    <h2>v6.3.0</h2>
    <h2>Behavior change: Java problem matcher is now opt-in</h2>
    <p>Starting with v6.3.0, <code>setup-java</code> no longer registers the
    Java problem matcher by default (<a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-java/issues/1326">#1326</a>,
    fixes <a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/actions/setup-java/issues/1322">#1322</a>).
    Java compiler warnings, compiler errors, and uncaught exceptions are no
    longer turned into annotations on pull request diffs unless you opt
    in.</p>
    <p>To keep annotations, set <code>problem-matcher: true</code>:</p>
    <pre lang="yaml"><code>- uses: actions/setup-java@v6
      with:
        distribution: temurin
        java-version: '25'
        problem-matcher: true
    </code></pre>
    <p>Compiler output still appears in the build logs, and compilation
    errors still fail the build. Only annotations are affected.</p>
    <p><strong>Why:</strong> inline annotations cluttered pull request
    reviews, and GitHub Actions caps annotations at 10 errors, 10 warnings,
    and 10 notices per step, and 50 per job. Larger Java builds therefore
    showed only a truncated subset of their diagnostics as annotations. See
    <a
    href="https://github.com/actions/setup-java/blob/main/docs/advanced-usage.md#java-problem-matcher-compiler-annotations">Java
    problem matcher (compiler annotations)</a>.</p>
